Zuli ProxyBroker Extended is an independently maintained derivative of the
upstream project proxybroker-rs (<https://github.com/TurtIeSocks/proxybroker-rs>).
Zuli claims only modifications to this distribution and does not claim
authorship of the upstream project. Original upstream copyright, attribution,
license notices, and prior statements of change remain preserved below.

Evidence-supported changes introduced by Zuli2021 in 2026 include:

  1. Distribution identity. The Cargo package is
     zuli-proxybroker-extended; the Rust library crate and CLI executable
     remain proxybroker.

  2. Proxy-pool and tunnel behavior. Initial proxy-pool fill concurrency and
     retry limits are configurable. Relay negotiation for HTTPS-capable
     upstream proxies used by HTTP CONNECT and SOCKS5 frontends was corrected
     to use opaque tunnels, a design intended to preserve client-owned
     end-to-end TLS.

  3. Focused automated tests cover pool-fill controls, CLI parsing, defaults,
     and relay-protocol selection.

  4. Distribution governance. Automatic crates.io publication was removed
     pending separate approval. The installer was retargeted to Zuli, made
     fail-closed for mandatory SHA-256 verification, and changed to retain
     LICENSE, NOTICE, and LICENSE-DATA. Release workflow logic was hardened
     for concurrency, publication ordering, stable/prerelease handling, and
     the GHCR latest-tag policy.

  5. Current-project README and mdBook documentation were migrated to the
     Zuli identity while preserving upstream provenance and historical records.

For engineering traceability, modified source files retain file-level
modification notices where established, while non-source distribution changes
are recorded in this NOTICE and the repository's Git history. Original upstream
notices remain preserved.

